/* Cloud assistant — free daily limit reached (spec 27ced9b / c259dc64).
   Names the assistant (Auris) and the free daily allowance; no invented reset
   time. "try again tomorrow" is the approved template wording. */
"cloud_error_limit_exceeded" = "Auris の無料の1日あたりの上限に達しました。明日もう一度お試しください。";

/* The conversation ended on the server, which is an ordinary end rather than a
   malfunction: say so plainly, and let the next request open a new conversation.
   Wording is shared with the other app so both say the same thing. */
"cloud_error_conversation_expired" = "その会話は終了しました。";

/* The answer did not come — the voice could not be produced, or the turn failed inside
   the assistant. To the listener these are one situation, so both codes speak this one
   sentence: an apology and a retry, with no system terms. Keep the two keys identical
   in every language; they are one line by decision, not two that may drift. */
"cloud_error_speech_unavailable" = "申し訳ありません。今はお答えできませんでした。もう一度お試しください。";
"cloud_error_internal_error" = "申し訳ありません。今はお答えできませんでした。もう一度お試しください。";
